        "name": "get_horn_state",
        "description": "Reports whether the Air Horner is sounding right now, whether it is looping, and whether audio is available in this browser. Read-only and side-effect free; safe to call at any time, including while stopped or mid-start, and it answers whatever the caller sends (arguments are ignored). Returns {playing, loop, hasAudioContext}."
      },
      {
        "name": "play_horn",
        "description": "Sound the Air Horner. Starts audio playback, pressed state and app badge, exactly like pressing the on-screen horn button. A call replaces anything already sounding (restarting the blast), and calls are rate limited, so repeated or concurrent invocations leave exactly one horn playing. Pass `loop: true` to keep it sounding until stop_horn is called, `loop: false` (the default) for a single blast. `loop` must be a real boolean: strings, numbers and objects are refused with a structured error rather than guessed at. Returns {playing, loop} when this call started the horn. A refused call returns {playing, loop, code, error} and changes nothing: code is one of invalid_input, audio_unavailable, not_started, rate_limited, timeout or internal, so treat a present code as the refusal and playing as the current state of the horn (it can already be sounding from an earlier call)."
      },
      {
        "name": "stop_horn",
        "description": "Silence the Air Horner immediately. Always honoured: it is never queued behind a start, rate limited, cancelled by an aborted call, or refused for bad arguments - silence must always be possible - so it is also safe to call when nothing is sounding. Takes no arguments; anything provided is ignored. Returns {playing: false, loop: false}."
      }
